schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-process-03-teaching-exploration-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-process
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: teaching-exploration-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook educator. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.Process. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Teach OTP process structure through safe runnable examples and concise comments.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.Process teaching and exploration cell that starts a small supervisor with named children, renders both top_down and left_right variants with Kino.Process.sup_tree/2, and traces a tiny Agent or GenServer message flow with Kino.Process.seq_trace/2. Add comments explaining app_tree/2 versus sup_tree/2, seq_trace/2, snapshot state, and how Process.info/2 plus Kino.DataTable can provide metrics.

    Requirements: include Livebook compatibility comments, fallback local supervisor creation, accessible text summaries, and safe execution checks. Do not require a real application to be attached. Do not use non-existent Kino.Process.info/1 or memory_usage/0. Keep tracing local and bounded.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-process-teaching-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino and renders sup_tree/2 variants plus a seq_trace/2 example."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and point-in-time diagram behavior."
  - "Reactive state: examples explain rerun or bounded animation for refreshed snapshots."
  - "Data shape: supervisor pids, registered names, child specs, traced messages, and metrics fields are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: summaries, labels, and local fallback process tree are present."
  - "Safe execution: no fake Kino.Process metric APIs, production tracing, remote node requirements, credentials, eval, or shell commands."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and starts local processes before rendering."
    - "Both layout examples and trace example use current public APIs."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Teaches sup_tree, app_tree, seq_trace, snapshot behavior, and Process.info metrics pairing."
    - "Uses only current Kino.Process APIs and standard Process metrics APIs."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Examples are scoped, readable, and ordered for learning."
    - "Text summaries explain what each process diagram means."
    - "Layout direction differences are easy to compare."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles already-started names, dead pids, empty traces, and missing local app context."
    - "Keeps process examples bounded and repeatable."
    - "Documents tracing overhead and refresh limitations."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.Process-centered and teaches safe OTP introspection."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-process
- teaching-exploration-widget

